    "id": "sunburst",
    "title": "Sunburst Chart",
    "category": "Composition",
    "description": "A sunburst chart shows a hierarchy as concentric rings: the inner ring is the top level, and each outer ring subdivides its parent into children, with arc angles proportional to value. Reading outward from the center traces a path down the hierarchy, and the width of each arc shows its share of its parent. It is a radial alternative to a treemap that makes the levels of nesting explicit.",
    "whenToUse": "Use it to reveal a multi-level part-to-whole hierarchy where you want the layers of nesting to be visually obvious, not just the leaf sizes.",
    "dataNeeded": [
      {
        "name": "Nested category level",
        "unit": "category"
      },
      {
        "name": "Value per node",
        "unit": "numeric"
      }
    ],
