    "id": "scatter-plot",
    "title": "Scatter Plot",
    "category": "Relationship",
    "description": "A scatter plot places one dot for each observation, using its two numeric values as the x and y coordinates. The overall cloud of dots reveals whether two variables move together: an upward-sloping band means they rise together, a downward band means one falls as the other rises, and a shapeless blob means no relationship. It is the workhorse for spotting correlation, clusters, and outliers.",
    "whenToUse": "Use it to check whether two numeric variables are related, to estimate the strength and direction of that relationship, and to catch outliers before running any statistics.",
    "dataNeeded": [
      {
        "name": "Explanatory variable (x)",
        "unit": "numeric"
      },
      {
        "name": "Response variable (y)",
        "unit": "numeric"
      }
    ],
