    "id": "choropleth-map",
    "title": "Choropleth Map",
    "category": "Specialized",
    "description": "A choropleth map shades geographic regions — countries, states, or counties — by the value of a variable, using color intensity to encode magnitude. It ties data to place, so you instantly see spatial patterns: clusters of dark regions, gradients across a continent, or a single bright outlier. Reading it means comparing shades against the legend to judge which areas are high or low.",
    "whenToUse": "Use it when your data is tied to defined geographic areas and you want to reveal regional patterns — population density, election results, or disease rates by region.",
    "dataNeeded": [
      {
        "name": "Geographic region",
        "unit": "category"
      },
      {
        "name": "Value per region",
        "unit": "numeric"
      }
    ],
