    "id": "gauge-chart",
    "title": "Gauge Chart",
    "category": "Specialized",
    "description": "A gauge chart shows a single value along a curved arc with a needle or filled sweep, styled like a speedometer, against a graded scale from minimum to maximum. It instantly communicates where one measurement sits relative to its range and any target zones, which is why dashboards use it for KPIs. The needle's angle within the colored bands tells you whether the value is in a good, warning, or critical zone.",
    "whenToUse": "Use it on a dashboard to display a single key metric against a known range or target, when the story is 'how close are we to the goal or the limit?'",
    "dataNeeded": [
      {
        "name": "Measured value",
        "unit": "numeric"
      },
      {
        "name": "Scale minimum",
        "unit": "numeric"
      },
      {
        "name": "Scale maximum",
        "unit": "numeric"
      }
    ],
