    "id": "area-chart",
    "title": "Area Chart",
    "category": "Trend",
    "description": "An area chart is a line chart with the region between the line and the baseline filled in, emphasizing the magnitude of the value over time rather than just its path. The shaded volume draws attention to totals and to how large the quantity is at each point. It suits a single series whose accumulation or level matters.",
    "whenToUse": "When you want to show a single value's trend over time while emphasizing its magnitude or volume beneath the line.",
