    "id": "line-chart",
    "title": "Line Chart",
    "category": "Trend",
    "description": "A line chart connects data points in order along a continuous axis (usually time) with straight segments, so the rise and fall of the line traces how a value changes. You read direction, rate, and turning points from the slope and shape of the line. The connected form implies the values are part of one evolving series.",
    "whenToUse": "When you want to show how a single continuous variable changes over an ordered axis such as time.",
    "dataNeeded": [
      {
        "name": "Time",
        "unit": "day"
      },
      {
        "name": "Value",
        "unit": "C"
      }
    ],
