    "id": "spline-chart",
    "title": "Spline Chart",
    "category": "Trend",
    "description": "A spline chart connects points with a smoothly curved line fitted through them rather than straight segments, giving a flowing, rounded trend. The curvature implies the underlying quantity varies continuously and gently between measurements. It reads well for naturally smooth phenomena but can overshoot or hide sharp real changes, so it should not be used when exact values between points matter.",
    "whenToUse": "When the underlying quantity is genuinely smooth and continuous and a flowing curve communicates the trend better than jagged segments.",
